{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"And Moab was afraid because of the people\"</b> — is because they were numerous, for Moab was small among the nations, since it is not an ancient people like the Canaanite and the Amorite and the rest of the descendants of Noah. And they were very afraid because of the people, for they were exceedingly numerous, for they multiplied and swarmed and grew strong beyond them. And they were further in dread of the children of Israel, because they heard of the great trials done for them and for their fathers. Now Moab knew that Israel would not conquer their land from them, for they had sent to them just as they sent to Sihon: \"until I cross the Jordan into the land that YHWH our Elohim gives us\" (Deuteronomy 2:29), or because they also heard of HaShem's prohibition when He said to them: \"Do not harass Moab\" (Deuteronomy 2:9). Therefore they said to the elders of Midian: Even though they will not conquer our land, in their multitude they will consume all the surroundings around us, as the ox consumes the green of the field, and they will conquer for themselves all our surroundings as they did to the two kings of the Amorites, and they will make us tributary servants:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:39.487689897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}